region in primates</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci USA</source><year>2005</year><volume>102</volume><fpage>9230</fpage><lpage>9234</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15967992</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1073/pnas.0500770102</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Watanabe</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Shiina</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Shimizu</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Hosomichi</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Yanagiya</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Kita</surname><given-names>YF</given-names></name><name><surname>Kimura</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Soeda</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Torii</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Ogasawara</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Kulski</surname><given-names>JK</given-names></name><name><surname>Inoko</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A BAC-based contig map of the cynomolgus macaque (Macaca fascicularis) major histocompatibility complex genomic region</article-title><source>Genomics</source><year>2007</year><volume>89</volume><fpage>402</fpage><lpage>412</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17174065</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.ygeno.2006.11.002</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Otting</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Heijmans</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Noort</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name><name><surname>de Groot</surname><given-names>NG</given-names></name><name><surname>Doxiadis</surname><given-names>GG</given-names></name><name><surname>van Rood</surname